["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Where grouse are in October depends on what happened in May. Learn the year once and every season makes sense.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 520\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Year wheel for grouse. January and February: winter, buds, needles and snow roosts. March to May: drumming, hooting and leks. May and June: nests, hatch in June. July and August: broods grow, adults moult. September and October: families split and young birds move. November and December: dusky grouse move uphill into conifers, winter starts. Region 3 general season: September 10 to November 30.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"520\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">The grouse year</text>\n<path d=\"M200 210 L200.0 60.0 A150 150 0 0 1 329.9 135.0 Z\" fill=\"#cfe0ef\" opacity=\"0.9\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 210 L329.9 135.0 A150 150 0 0 1 275.0 339.9 Z\" fill=\"#e9c46a\" opacity=\"0.9\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 210 L329.9 285.0 A150 150 0 0 1 200.0 360.0 Z\" fill=\"#f2b38f\" opacity=\"0.9\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 210 L200.0 360.0 A150 150 0 0 1 70.1 285.0 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" opacity=\"0.9\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 210 L70.1 285.0 A150 150 0 0 1 70.1 135.0 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\"0.9\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 210 L70.1 135.0 A150 150 0 0 1 200.0 60.0 Z\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" opacity=\"0.9\"/>\n<circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"210\" r=\"78\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"230.28182827699493\" y=\"102.98667832417901\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">J</text>\n<text x=\"282.73149339882605\" y=\"133.26850660117395\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">F</text>\n<text x=\"313.013321675821\" y=\"185.71817172300507\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">M</text>\n<text x=\"313.013321675821\" y=\"246.28182827699493\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A</text>\n<text x=\"282.73149339882605\" y=\"298.73149339882605\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">M</text>\n<text x=\"230.28182827699496\" y=\"329.013321675821\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">J</text>\n<text x=\"169.71817172300507\" y=\"329.013321675821\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">J</text>\n<text x=\"117.26850660117395\" y=\"298.73149339882605\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A</text>\n<text x=\"86.98667832417901\" y=\"246.28182827699493\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">S</text>\n<text x=\"86.986678324179\" y=\"185.71817172300513\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">O</text>\n<text x=\"117.26850660117393\" y=\"133.26850660117395\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">N</text>\n<text x=\"169.71817172300507\" y=\"102.98667832417901\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">D</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Season</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"209\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Sept 10 to</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"228\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Nov 30 (R3)</text>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"369\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#cfe0ef\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"38\" y=\"382\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Winter: buds, needles, snow roosts</text>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"391\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#e9c46a\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"38\" y=\"404\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Drumming, hooting, leks</text>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"413\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f2b38f\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"38\" y=\"426\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Nests, hatch in June</text>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"435\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"38\" y=\"448\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Broods grow, moult</text>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"457\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"38\" y=\"470\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Families split, young move</text>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"479\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"38\" y=\"492\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Uphill, into conifers</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Spring: drumming and hooting. June: hatch <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Fall: families split, dusky grouse go uphill (75 to 80%).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the year in one table</summary><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Months</th><th>What happens</th><th>Certainty</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Jan, Feb</td><td>Buds and needles, snow roosts, hardest survival</td><td>75 to 85%</td></tr><tr><td>Mar to May</td><td>Ruffed drum, dusky and sooty hoot, sharp tails dance, spruce strut</td><td>75 to 85%</td></tr><tr><td>May, Jun</td><td>Nests; ruffed hatch usually early June</td><td>85%</td></tr><tr><td>Jul, Aug</td><td>Chicks grow on insects then plants; adults moult</td><td>75 to 85%</td></tr><tr><td>Sep, Oct</td><td>Families split, young birds disperse</td><td>75 to 80%</td></tr><tr><td>Oct, Nov</td><td>Dusky and sooty move uphill to dense conifers; ptarmigan turn white</td><td>70 to 85%</td></tr><tr><td>Dec</td><td>Winter food, snow roosts start</td><td>75%</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details>","<div class=\"gallery\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-aspen-grove-snow.jpg\" alt=\"Aspen in winter: buds feed ruffed grouse.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Aspen in winter: buds feed ruffed grouse. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Jason Hollinger, CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aspen_Grove_in_Snow_(2276157824).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-subalpine-forest.jpg\" alt=\"Spruce and pine: needles feed spruce grouse.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Spruce and pine: needles feed spruce grouse. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Tim Gage at Flickr, CC BY-SA 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Picea_engelmannii_Pinus_contorta.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure></div><ul><li>Ruffed grouse eat buds; spruce and dusky eat needles (80 to 85%).</li><li>January to March is when most birds die <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: winter detail</summary><ul><li>Ruffed grouse: buds and catkins of poplar, aspen, birch and alder (85%, Hinterland Who's Who); aspen flower buds preferred <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Spruce grouse: up to 99% conifer needles in the snow season <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Dusky grouse: conifer needles, often high in Douglas fir (70 to 75%).</li><li>Sharp tailed grouse: buds and catkins of deciduous trees and shrubs (85%, BC species account).</li><li>Ptarmigan: willow, alder and birch buds; white tailed ptarmigan also eat conifer needles <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Survival is lowest January to March (75%, Maine study). Monthly survival 80 to 90% then (75%, Pennsylvania).</li><li>No hunting season in these months for these birds in your regions (99%, <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-3/12\">Rule Book</a>).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation of a male ruffed grouse drumming on a mossy log. He stands tall on the log with his tail braced and beats his cupped wings forward and back. The beats start slow, thump, thump, then speed up into a whirr of about 50 beats in 8 to 10 seconds. The sound comes from the wings beating the air, not from hitting the log.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">The drum: a feathered engine</text>\n<rect x=\"60\" y=\"214\" width=\"290\" height=\"30\" rx=\"15\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><ellipse cx=\"350\" cy=\"229\" rx=\"10\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#a8835b\"/>\n<path d=\"M70 214 q30 -8 60 0 q40 -8 70 0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"5\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(200 170)\"><polygon points=\"-26,-6 -56,-30 -66,-6 -60,14 -26,10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"28\" ry=\"20\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"-44\" width=\"11\" height=\"34\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-50\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"12,-57 16,-68 22,-57\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"25,-52 34,-49 25,-46\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"-52\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><ellipse cx=\"14\" cy=\"-22\" rx=\"9\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M0 18 l-2 26 M10 18 l2 26\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(206 168)\"><path d=\"M0 0 Q40 -10 46 30 Q20 24 0 10 Z\" fill=\"#7a5233\"><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" values=\"0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;-70;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0.0000;0.0375;0.0688;0.1500;0.1812;0.2378;0.2690;0.3062;0.3329;0.3596;0.3804;0.4012;0.4175;0.4337;0.4464;0.4590;0.4689;0.4788;0.4865;0.4942;0.5002;0.5062;0.5109;0.5156;0.5200;0.5244;0.5287;0.5331;0.5375;0.5419;0.5462;0.5506;0.5550;0.5594;0.5637;0.5681;0.5725;0.5769;0.5812;0.5856;0.5900;0.5944;0.5987;0.6031;0.6075;0.6119;0.6162;0.6206;0.6250;0.6294;0.6337;0.6381;0.6425;0.6469;0.6512;0.6556;0.6600;0.6644;0.6687;0.6731;0.6775;0.6819;0.6862;0.6906;0.6950;0.6994;0.7037;0.7081;0.7125;0.7169;0.7212;0.7256;0.7300;0.7344;0.7387;0.7431;0.7475;0.7519;0.7562;0.7606;0.7650;0.7694;0.7737;0.7781;0.7825;0.7869;0.7912;0.7956;0.8000;0.8044;0.8087;1.0000\" dur=\"8s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></path></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"0.2s\"/><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"3s\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Thump ... thump ...</text></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"3s\"/><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"5.5s\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Faster: thump thump thump</text></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"5.5s\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A whirr: about 50 beats in 8 to 10 s</text></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"8s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"256\" width=\"360\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"279\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Cupped wings beat the air, not the log</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>A ruffed grouse drumming: slow, then a whirr. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"video\"><video controls preload=\"none\" playsinline src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/43/Ruff_Grouse_Drumming.webm/Ruff_Grouse_Drumming.webm.480p.vp9.webm\"></video><figcaption>Hear the drum: a ruffed grouse beating its wings. <span class=\"credit\">Video: Dale Bohlke, CC BY 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ruff_Grouse_Drumming.webm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a>. Needs internet.</span></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Ruffed males drum from a log, mostly March to May (75 to 85%).</li><li>The wings beat the air; they do not hit the log <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: drumming, every number we found</summary><ul><li>The male stands on a log, braces with his tail and snaps his cupped wings forward and back (85%, Hinterland Who's Who).</li><li>The beats start slow and speed into a whirr (75%, Pennsylvania Game Commission). About 50 beats in about 8 to 10 seconds (65%, Nova Scotia and Saltscapes accounts).</li><li>The sound is very low, under 100 Hz <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>, and can be heard about 400 m or more in thick woods (60 to 70%). How far depends on which way the bird faces (70%, Archibald 1974).</li><li>Peak drumming is in spring; in one study the peak was mid April <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>. Pennsylvania gives March and April <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Males also drum in fall (85%, Hinterland Who's Who) and a little all year <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Why: to warn off other males and draw hens <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Field use: in April, listen at dawn from a quiet road and map every drummer. Those territories hold birds in October (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 340\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Four spring displays. Ruffed grouse: drums on a log at dawn from March to May, and a little again in fall. Spruce grouse: struts with red combs up and tail fanned, makes a short flight and two loud wing claps. Dusky and sooty grouse: deep hoots with neck air sacs showing; the sooty hoots from high in a conifer. Sharp tailed grouse: dances on a lek at dawn, stamping its feet, rattling its tail and showing pink neck sacs.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"340\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Spring shows: 4 grouse, 4 acts</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"42\" width=\"185\" height=\"140\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Ruffed: drums</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">On a log at dawn,</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">March to May. Again</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"152\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">a little in fall.</text>\n<g transform=\"translate(155 88) scale(0.6 0.6)\"><polygon points=\"-20,-6 -38,-20 -48,-12 -52,0 -48,8 -20,8\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M-40 -18 Q-50 -10 -48 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"16,-20 20,-28 25,-20\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n<rect x=\"205\" y=\"42\" width=\"185\" height=\"140\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"215\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Spruce: struts</text>\n<text x=\"215\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Red combs up, tail</text>\n<text x=\"215\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">fanned, short flight,</text>\n<text x=\"215\" y=\"152\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">two loud wing claps.</text>\n<g transform=\"translate(350 88) scale(0.6 0.6)\"><polygon points=\"-22,-4 -36,-8 -36,4 -22,6\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#3d3a35\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#3d3a35\"/><path d=\"M18 -20 q5 -5 10 0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#c23b22\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"192\" width=\"185\" height=\"140\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"216\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Dusky, sooty: hoots</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Deep hoots, neck sacs</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">show. Sooty hoots</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"302\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">high in a conifer.</text>\n<g transform=\"translate(155 238) scale(0.6 0.6)\"><polygon points=\"-22,-4 -50,-10 -50,4 -22,7\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#5d6670\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#5d6670\"/><path d=\"M18 -20 q5 -5 10 0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e3a21a\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n<rect x=\"205\" y=\"192\" width=\"185\" height=\"140\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"215\" y=\"216\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Sharp tail: dances</text>\n<text x=\"215\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">On a lek at dawn.</text>\n<text x=\"215\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Stamp, rattle tail,</text>\n<text x=\"215\" y=\"302\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">pink neck sacs.</text>\n<g transform=\"translate(350 238) scale(0.6 0.6)\"><polygon points=\"-22,-3 -48,-2 -22,6\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#b89a74\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#b89a74\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n</svg>\n</figure><figure class=\"video\"><video controls preload=\"none\" playsinline src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/2e/Dusky_Grouse.webm/Dusky_Grouse.webm.480p.vp9.webm\"></video><figcaption>A male dusky grouse showing off for a hen. <span class=\"credit\">Video: Nomdeploom, CC0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dusky_Grouse.webm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a>. Needs internet.</span></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Dusky and sooty hoot; spruce struts and claps; sharp tails dance (65 to 85%).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: each display</summary><ul><li>Dusky grouse: males inflate neck air sacs and give deep owl like hoots, heard up to about 400 m (75%, Idaho Fish and Game). The sound is so low you may feel it before you hear it <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>. Hooting runs late March to mid July <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Sooty grouse: males hoot from high in a conifer, a run of about six deep hoots that can carry about 800 m <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Dusky grouse leave the high country in late March or early April for breeding ground lower down (70%, Colorado Parks and Wildlife).</li><li>Spruce grouse: males strut with red combs up and tail fanned, then make a short flight that ends in two loud wing claps (65 to 75%).</li><li>Sharp tailed grouse: males dance on a lek at dawn, stamp their feet, rattle their tails and show pink neck sacs <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>. Lek calls carry up to 1.5 km (85%, BC species account). Leks are used for many years if left undisturbed <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Ptarmigan males display with red combs: willow gargle, rock snore, white tailed scream (85%, Hinterland Who's Who).</li><li>Respect: disturbance at leks can make hens abandon them <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>. Watch from far away.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Eggs per nest. Spruce grouse in Alberta, the Franklin form: 4.8 on average. Dusky grouse: 7 to 9 on average. Ruffed grouse: 7 to 12. Ptarmigan: 5 to 14. Sharp tailed grouse in BC: 12.8 on average. Eggs hatch after about 3 weeks, 21 to 24 days.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Eggs per nest (average or range)</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Spruce (Alberta)</text>\n<rect x=\"125.6\" y=\"64\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"143.6\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">4.8 avg</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"102\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Dusky</text>\n<rect x=\"174\" y=\"108\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"226\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">7 to 9 avg</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"146\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Ruffed</text>\n<rect x=\"174\" y=\"152\" width=\"110\" height=\"16\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"292\" y=\"166\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">7 to 12</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Ptarmigan</text>\n<rect x=\"130\" y=\"196\" width=\"198\" height=\"16\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"336\" y=\"210\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">5 to 14</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"234\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Sharp tailed (BC)</text>\n<rect x=\"301.6\" y=\"240\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"319.6\" y=\"254\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">12.8 avg</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Eggs hatch after about 3 weeks (21 to 24 days).</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Ruffed: 7 to 12 eggs, hatch usually early June <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Chicks leave the nest within a day <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: nests, eggs and chicks</summary><ul><li>Ruffed grouse: 7 to 12 eggs, incubation 23 to 24 days, hatch usually early June (85%, Hinterland Who's Who). Pennsylvania gives 6 to 16 eggs, about 24 days <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Spruce grouse: clutches average 4.8 in Alberta, the Franklin's form <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. Median hatch there about 29 June <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. Chicks fly short hops at about 6 days <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Dusky grouse: about 7 to 9 eggs on average <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>, chicks hatch late May to early June <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Sharp tailed grouse: first clutch at 11 months old, average 12.8 eggs, one brood a year, often renest if the nest fails (85%, BC species account). Most nests within 1.6 km of a lek <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Ptarmigan: 5 to 14 eggs, about 3 weeks <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>. Chicks fly clumsily at about a week <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Only the hen sits on the eggs in ruffed grouse <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. Male willow ptarmigan stay and help <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"gallery\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-huckleberry-bush.jpg\" alt=\"Huckleberry: summer food for dusky grouse.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Huckleberry: summer food for dusky grouse. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Katja Schulz from Washington, D. C., USA, CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mountain_Huckleberry_(14891686107).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-saskatoon-berries.jpg\" alt=\"Saskatoon berries: summer and fall food.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Saskatoon berries: summer and fall food. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Thayne Tuason, CC BY 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amelanchier-alnifolia-var-cusickii-unripe-fruit_8795424698_o_2.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure></div><ul><li>Chicks eat insects first, then leaves, flowers and berries <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Adults moult their flight feathers (75 to 85%).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: summer detail</summary><ul><li>Ruffed chicks eat insects first; by August flowers, soft leaves, berries and seeds; clover is a favourite (85%, Hinterland Who's Who).</li><li>Chicks make low, buzzy flights in week 1 and fly well by week 3 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Yearling plumage by 16 to 17 weeks <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Adults moult once a year: Hinterland Who's Who says from June, Pennsylvania July into September (75 to 85%).</li><li>Dusky grouse males leave breeding areas by mid July for high forest with huckleberry (70%, Colorado Parks and Wildlife).</li><li>Dog training on game birds under supervision is allowed from 1 August (99%, <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods/15\">Rule Book</a>).</li></ul></details><aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 439\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Season bar chart: Region 3 grouse and ptarmigan. Dusky, ruffed, spruce grouse: 3-12 to 3-20, 3-26 to 3-44: Sept 10 to Nov 30. Dusky, ruffed, spruce grouse: 3-46: Sept 20 to Nov 30. Grouse, Youth Only: 3-12 to 3-20, 3-26 to 3-44: Sept 1 to Sept 9. New, printed green. Sharp tailed grouse: ✻3-30, 3-31: Sept 10 to Nov 30. ✻ Map C18 closure. Ptarmigan: 3-12 to 3-20, 3-26 to 3-44: Sept 1 to Nov 30.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"439\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Region 3 grouse and ptarmigan</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"47\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Page 34.</text>\n<text x=\"74.0\" y=\"83\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sep</text>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"83\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Oct</text>\n<text x=\"326.0\" y=\"83\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Nov</text>\n<line x1=\"12.0\" y1=\"91\" x2=\"12.0\" y2=\"429\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.6\"/>\n<line x1=\"136.0\" y1=\"91\" x2=\"136.0\" y2=\"429\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.6\"/>\n<line x1=\"264.0\" y1=\"91\" x2=\"264.0\" y2=\"429\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.6\"/>\n<line x1=\"388.0\" y1=\"91\" x2=\"388.0\" y2=\"429\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\"0.6\"/>\n<text x=\"12\" y=\"107\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Dusky, ruffed, spruce grouse: 3-12 to 3-20,</text>\n<text x=\"12\" y=\"125\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">3-26 to 3-44</text>\n<rect x=\"49.2\" y=\"131\" width=\"338.8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"218.6\" y=\"147\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sept 10 to Nov 30</text>\n<text x=\"12\" y=\"181\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Dusky, ruffed, spruce grouse: 3-46</text>\n<rect x=\"90.5\" y=\"187\" width=\"297.5\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"239.3\" y=\"203\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sept 20 to Nov 30</text>\n<text x=\"12\" y=\"237\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Grouse, Youth Only: 3-12 to 3-20, 3-26 to 3-44</text>\n<rect x=\"12.0\" y=\"243\" width=\"37.2\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"55.2\" y=\"259\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Sept 1 to Sept 9</text>\n<text x=\"12\" y=\"283\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\">New, printed green</text>\n<text x=\"12\" y=\"315\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Sharp tailed grouse: ✻3-30, 3-31</text>\n<rect x=\"49.2\" y=\"321\" width=\"338.8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"218.6\" y=\"337\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sept 10 to Nov 30</text>\n<text x=\"12\" y=\"361\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\">✻ Map C18 closure</text>\n<text x=\"12\" y=\"393\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Ptarmigan: 3-12 to 3-20, 3-26 to 3-44</text>\n<rect x=\"12.0\" y=\"399\" width=\"376.0\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"415\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sept 1 to Nov 30</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Broods break up; young birds wander <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Region 3: youth 1 to 9 Sept, everyone from 10 Sept <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: September detail and dates</summary><ul><li>Families split at about 12 weeks; young birds disperse over 2 to 3 weeks, hens farther than males (75 to 80%).</li><li>Restless young birds turn up in odd places, roads and yards <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Region 3, MUs (Management Units) 3-12 to 3-20 and 3-26 to 3-44: youth only (under 18) 1 to 9 September; general 10 September to 30 November (99%, <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-3/12\">Rule Book</a>).</li><li>Region 3 ptarmigan: 1 September to 30 November <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Region 2: bow only 1 to 9 September; general 10 September to 15 December (99%, <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-2/10\">Rule Book</a>).</li><li>Region 8: youth 1 to 9 September; general 10 September to 30 November; bow only 1 to 10 December (99%, <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-8/10\">Rule Book</a>).</li><li>Sharp tailed grouse, Region 3, MUs 3-30 and 3-31: 10 September to 30 November <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul></details><aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two panels. Early October: young birds on edges eating clover, berries and grit; leaves are still up, so shots are short and fast. Late November: snow lets you read tracks, birds sit in conifers eating buds and needles, and with the leaves down you can see far.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">October vs late November</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"40\" width=\"185\" height=\"250\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fbf1dc\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<rect x=\"205\" y=\"40\" width=\"185\" height=\"250\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#eef3f7\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"102\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Early October</text>\n<text x=\"298\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Late November</text>\n<rect x=\"57\" y=\"128\" width=\"6\" height=\"34\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><ellipse cx=\"60\" cy=\"114\" rx=\"21\" ry=\"24\" fill=\"#e9c46a\"/>\n<rect x=\"137\" y=\"133\" width=\"6\" height=\"29\" fill=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><ellipse cx=\"140\" cy=\"121\" rx=\"18\" ry=\"21\" fill=\"#e9a03a\"/>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"160\" width=\"185\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(100 150) scale(0.5 0.5)\"><polygon points=\"-20,-6 -38,-20 -48,-12 -52,0 -48,8 -20,8\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M-40 -18 Q-50 -10 -48 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"16,-20 20,-28 25,-20\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Young birds on edges</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Clover, berries, grit</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"232\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Leaves still up:</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">short, fast shots</text>\n<polygon points=\"250,80 214.0,160 286.0,160\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"247\" y=\"160\" width=\"6\" height=\"12\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/>\n<polygon points=\"330,70 289.5,160 370.5,160\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"327\" y=\"160\" width=\"6\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/>\n<rect x=\"205\" y=\"160\" width=\"185\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#b9c6d3\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(300 108) scale(0.45 0.45)\"><polygon points=\"-22,-4 -50,-10 -50,4 -22,7\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#5d6670\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#5d6670\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n<text x=\"215\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Snow: read tracks</text>\n<text x=\"215\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Birds in conifers</text>\n<text x=\"215\" y=\"232\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Buds and needles</text>\n<text x=\"215\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Leaves down: see far</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>October: young birds on edges, clover and berries <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>November: birds tighter in conifers, dusky high, snow tells all (70 to 80%).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what changes, week by week</summary><ul><li>Early October: leaves still up, short shots. Young birds feed on road edges and cut blocks <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Fall drumming: you may hear ruffed males drum on calm October mornings (85% that they drum in fall; timing Tip).</li><li>Dusky and sooty grouse move uphill into dense conifers and switch to needles (70 to 75%). Some travel tens of kilometres; most much less <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Sharp tailed grouse move to deciduous cover, berries, then buds; late flocks get big and wild (60 to 85%).</li><li>Ptarmigan are mostly white by mid October <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>, easy to see on brown rock before snow and hard to see after (Tip).</li><li>First snows: grouse sit in conifers and leave tracks (Tip).</li><li>By late November more of the birds left are adults <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Region 3 and Region 8 seasons close 30 November; Region 2 runs to 15 December <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Old hand's rule (tradition): \"Leaves down, birds up\": after leaf fall you see farther and get more open shots.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"gallery\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-grouse-snow-roost.jpg\" alt=\"Snow roost hole with wing marks.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Snow roost hole with wing marks. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Cephas, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bonasa_umbellus_snow_hole.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-grouse-tracks-snow.jpg\" alt=\"Tracks in soft snow.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Tracks in soft snow. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Yellowstone National Park, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ruffed_grouse_tracks_in_snow_(49522761717).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure></div><ul><li>Snow roosts start once snow is soft and deep enough (70 to 75%).</li></ul>","<ul><li>Region 2 open to 15 Dec; Region 8 bow only 1 to 10 Dec <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: December detail</summary><ul><li>Ruffed grouse dive into snow about 20 to 40 cm deep to roost (70 to 75%).</li><li>Hard crust or thin snow pushes birds into thick conifers <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Region 2 grouse: open to 15 December <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Region 8: bow only 1 to 10 December <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Region 3: closed after 30 November <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul></details><aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 520\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Year wheel for grouse. January and February: winter, buds, needles and snow roosts. March to May: drumming, hooting and leks. May and June: nests, hatch in June. July and August: broods grow, adults moult. September and October: families split and young birds move. November and December: dusky grouse move uphill into conifers, winter starts. Region 3 general season: September 10 to November 30.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"520\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">The grouse year</text>\n<path d=\"M200 210 L200.0 60.0 A150 150 0 0 1 329.9 135.0 Z\" fill=\"#cfe0ef\" opacity=\"0.9\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 210 L329.9 135.0 A150 150 0 0 1 275.0 339.9 Z\" fill=\"#e9c46a\" opacity=\"0.9\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 210 L329.9 285.0 A150 150 0 0 1 200.0 360.0 Z\" fill=\"#f2b38f\" opacity=\"0.9\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 210 L200.0 360.0 A150 150 0 0 1 70.1 285.0 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" opacity=\"0.9\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 210 L70.1 285.0 A150 150 0 0 1 70.1 135.0 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\"0.9\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 210 L70.1 135.0 A150 150 0 0 1 200.0 60.0 Z\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" opacity=\"0.9\"/>\n<circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"210\" r=\"78\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"230.28182827699493\" y=\"102.98667832417901\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">J</text>\n<text x=\"282.73149339882605\" y=\"133.26850660117395\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">F</text>\n<text x=\"313.013321675821\" y=\"185.71817172300507\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">M</text>\n<text x=\"313.013321675821\" y=\"246.28182827699493\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A</text>\n<text x=\"282.73149339882605\" y=\"298.73149339882605\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">M</text>\n<text x=\"230.28182827699496\" y=\"329.013321675821\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">J</text>\n<text x=\"169.71817172300507\" y=\"329.013321675821\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">J</text>\n<text x=\"117.26850660117395\" y=\"298.73149339882605\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A</text>\n<text x=\"86.98667832417901\" y=\"246.28182827699493\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">S</text>\n<text x=\"86.986678324179\" y=\"185.71817172300513\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">O</text>\n<text x=\"117.26850660117393\" y=\"133.26850660117395\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">N</text>\n<text x=\"169.71817172300507\" y=\"102.98667832417901\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">D</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Season</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"209\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Sept 10 to</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"228\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Nov 30 (R3)</text>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"369\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#cfe0ef\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"38\" y=\"382\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Winter: buds, needles, snow roosts</text>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"391\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#e9c46a\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"38\" y=\"404\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Drumming, hooting, leks</text>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"413\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f2b38f\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"38\" y=\"426\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Nests, hatch in June</text>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"435\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"38\" y=\"448\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Broods grow, moult</text>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"457\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"38\" y=\"470\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Families split, young move</text>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"479\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"38\" y=\"492\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Uphill, into conifers</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Rhyme: \"April drums, June chicks come, September splits, December's numb.\"</li><li>Number trick: \"7 to 12 eggs, 24 days\": ruffed clutch and incubation.</li><li>Old hand's rule (tradition): \"Find the drummer in April, find the bird in October.\"</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li>\"Dusky goes up when the leaves come down.\"</li><li>\"12 weeks to split, 3 weeks to fly.\"</li><li>\"Season 10 to 30\": Region 3 opens 10 September, closes 30 November.</li><li>\"Ptarmigan white by mid October.\"</li><li>The drummer rule is widely repeated grouse hunting advice; rhymes are made for this course.</li></ul></details>","<ul><li>Hinterland Who's Who, Pennsylvania Game Commission, BC species account, Rule Book. Checked 2026-10-11.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every source</summary><ul><li>Rule Book: <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-3/12\">Region 3</a>, <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-2/10\">Region 2</a>, <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-8/10\">Region 8</a>, <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods/15\">dogs</a>. Synopsis 2 October 2026 edition <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.hww.ca/en/wildlife/birds/ruffed-grouse.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Hinterland Who's Who, Ruffed grouse</a> and <a href=\"https://www.hww.ca/assets/pdfs/factsheets/ptarmigan-en.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ptarmigan</a>, read directly <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.pa.gov/agencies/pgc/wildlife/discover-pa-wildlife/ruffed-grouse\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Pennsylvania Game Commission, Ruffed grouse</a>, read directly <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.env.gov.bc.ca/wld/frpa/iwms/documents/Birds/b_columbiansharptailedgrouse.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC species account, Columbian Sharp tailed Grouse</a>, read directly <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://idfg.idaho.gov/press/field-forest-grouse\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Idaho Fish and Game</a> <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span> and <a href=\"https://wildaboututah.org/western-forest-grouse/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Wild About Utah</a> <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>, read directly.</li><li><a href=\"https://sora.unm.edu/sites/default/files/journals/auk/v091n03/p0517-p0521.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Archibald 1974, The Auk 91</a> and drumming peak study (Southeastern Association of Fish and Wildlife Agencies), search preview (70 to 80%).</li><li>Nova Scotia and Saltscapes drumming accounts, search preview <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Spruce grouse clutch and hatch: The Condor 77 papers, search preview <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Colorado Parks and Wildlife, dusky grouse; Audubon, dusky grouse, read 2026-10-03 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Sooty grouse hooting: Birdweb, search preview <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Dendragapus_obscurus/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Animal Diversity Web, dusky grouse</a>, read directly <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>All checked 2026-10-11 unless noted. Full log: <code>research/2026-10-11-masterclass-grouse.md</code>.</li></ul></details>"]